.TH TUX-BURNERD 8 "October 2026" "Tux Burner 0.99" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
tux-burnerd \- Tux Burner root hardware service
.SH DESCRIPTION
The root daemon that performs every GPU write for Tux Burner (voltage offset, clocks, power cap,
fan curve) and runs the saved-profile engine. It listens on /run/tux-burnerd.sock and is started as
.BR tux-burnerd.service .
Install or repair the service with
.BR "tburn-cli --install-systemd-service" ;
remove it with
.BR "tburn-cli --uninstall-systemd-service" .
.PP
On AMD it enforces its own VDDGFX safety floor, independent of the GUI and CLI: default \-150 mV,
changed through /etc/tux-burner/amd-vddgfx-floor-mv or the environment variable
TUX_BURNERD_AMD_VDDGFX_FLOOR_MV in the unit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/tux-burner/amd-vddgfx-floor-mv
.TP
.I /var/lib/tux-burner/
.TP
.I /var/opt/tux-burner/libexec/tux-burnerd
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tburn-cli (1)
